# Windows batch and command scripts must be checked out with CRLF line
# endings. cmd.exe's parser uses absolute file offsets and re-seeks across
# line boundaries; LF-only .bat files containing multi-line if/for blocks
# can send it into an infinite loop reading partial tokens (e.g. `setlocal`
# becoming `ocal` after the first re-seek). Enforce CRLF here regardless
# of each contributor's local core.autocrlf setting.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
